1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,060
The Moon is quietly
holding our seasons steady.

2
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:04,182
Here's how.

3
00:00:04,972 --> 00:00:07,304
Earth's tilt is what
gives us seasons.

4
00:00:07,394 --> 00:00:10,168
Today it only rocks between
about twenty-two and

5
00:00:10,188 --> 00:00:12,242
twenty-four and
a half degrees.

6
00:00:13,032 --> 00:00:15,420
The Moon drives about
two-thirds of the slow

7
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:16,949
wobble of Earth's axis.

8
00:00:17,739 --> 00:00:21,205
Without it, a 1993 study
found the tilt could

9
00:00:21,225 --> 00:00:24,536
wander chaotically,
from near zero to about

10
00:00:24,556 --> 00:00:26,355
eighty-five degrees.

11
00:00:27,145 --> 00:00:29,882
A 2011 study found
narrower swings,

12
00:00:29,902 --> 00:00:32,358
about ten to
twenty degrees.

13
00:00:32,448 --> 00:00:34,625
Still enough to redraw
the world's climate

14
00:00:34,645 --> 00:00:35,209
zones.

15
00:00:35,999 --> 00:00:38,605
Either way, the Moon is
a hand on the steering

16
00:00:38,625 --> 00:00:40,074
wheel of our seasons.

17
00:00:40,164 --> 00:00:41,628
Full story on
our channel.
